: OpenRouter's shape for image-output models on the OpenAI-compatible
: endpoint: delta.images, each entry a data URI, arriving in the same delta as
: the text. Text and image both have to survive, and the image is streamed
: live rather than held for the final chunk.
:
: A keep-alive comment leads the stream, because that is what a real
: connection sends while the model is still thinking and it must not be
: mistaken for a payload.
:
: Transcribed from
: openai::tests::decodes_generated_images_from_the_delta_images_array and
: openai::tests::malformed_lines_and_comments_are_skipped.

: keep-alive

data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"here you go","images":[{"type":"image_url","image_url":{"url":"data:image/png;base64,QUJD"}}]},"finish_reason":"stop"}]}

data: [DONE]

